{"event":"intent","sources":["origin","f001"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s01; BRANCH=rx-pull-stale-hdr; Search only snapshots/s01 and never open any other snapshot. Direct structural/API analogue of the seed: receive-path protocol parsers (net/* *_rcv, *_recv, *_do_rcv, *_rx handlers) that capture a header pointer with skb_header_pointer() or a direct skb->data cast, then call pskb_may_pull()/pskb_pull()/pskb_pull_reserve()/__pskb_pull_tail()/skb_linearize() in the same function scope, and afterwards read or write through the stale pointer without refetching — the pep_get_sb() pattern where ph stayed live across pskb_may_pull(skb, ph->sb_len) and was then read via ph->sb_type and written via ph->sb_len -= 2. Flag cases where the pull length itself comes from the attacker-controlled header. For each candidate record exact file:function:line evidence (pointer capture, reallocating pull, every post-pull dereference); if none, record an evidence-backed negative of what was searched. Save a structured artifact for snapshot s01 only."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["origin","f001"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s01; BRANCH=tx-cow-head-realloc; Search only snapshots/s01 and never open any other snapshot. Lifetime/ownership analogue on transmit and edit paths: tunnel xmit handlers, neighbor/ndisc output, netfilter mangle and targets, encapsulation, header push/pull edits, and similar code that caches a pointer into skb head/data or into network/MAC/private headers and then calls a helper documented to reallocate or replace the head buffer — skb_cow_head(), skb_cow(), skb_unclone(), skb_share_check(), pskb_expand_head(), skb_linearize() — and dereferences the old pointer afterwards without refetching from skb->data; pskb_expand_head() frees the old head, so every pre-call pointer is a use-after-free. Record exact file:function:line evidence (capture, reallocating call, stale use) for each candidate, or an evidence-backed negative. Save a structured artifact for snapshot s01 only."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["origin","f001"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s01; BRANCH=loop-parser-stale-state; Search only snapshots/s01 and never open any other snapshot. Equivalent data-flow invariant in a different shape: variable-length record/TLV/option/attribute parse loops and 'get next record' helpers where pskb_may_pull()/pskb_pull()/__pskb_pull_tail()/skb_linearize() executes inside the loop body or inside a per-iteration helper while pointer, cursor, offset, or length state captured before the pull (outer scope or earlier iteration) stays live and is dereferenced in a later iteration or after the helper returns — the seed's pep_get_sb() is exactly such a helper. Distinguish from single-pass parsers: the stale state here crosses an iteration or call boundary. Record exact file:function:line evidence of the captured state, the interior pull, and the stale dereference, or an evidence-backed negative. Save a structured artifact for snapshot s01 only."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["origin","f001"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s01; BRANCH=gro-frag-stale-ptr; Search only snapshots/s01 and never open any other snapshot. Cross-subsystem GRO/segmentation/frag-list analogue: *_gro_receive/*_gro_complete handlers, GSO segmenters, and frag-list walkers that hold pointers into per-packet headers — skb_gro_header_pointer()/skb_gro_header_slow() results, gro network-header pointers, pointers into frag-list or skb_shinfo data — across skb_gro_pull(), pskb_may_pull() over frag lists, skb_gro_receive(), or other head-relocation/frag-consumption, and dereference them afterwards without re-fetching via skb_gro_header_fast()/skb_gro_header_slow(). Record exact file:function:line evidence (capture, relocating call, stale use) for each candidate or an evidence-backed negative of what was searched. Save a structured artifact for snapshot s01 only."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["origin","f001"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s02; BRANCH=rx-pull-stale-hdr; Search only snapshots/s02 and never open any other snapshot. Direct structural/API analogue of the seed: receive-path protocol parsers (net/* *_rcv, *_recv, *_do_rcv, *_rx handlers) that cache a header pointer via skb_header_pointer() or a direct skb->data cast before pskb_may_pull()/pskb_pull()/__pskb_pull_tail()/skb_linearize() and then read or write through that stale pointer after the pull without refetching, as in pep_get_sb() where ph outlived pskb_may_pull(skb, ph->sb_len). Watch for non-linear skb handling and for pulls whose length argument is itself read from the untrusted header. Record exact file:function:line evidence — pointer capture, reallocating pull, every post-pull dereference — or an evidence-backed negative of what was searched. Save a structured artifact for snapshot s02 only."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["origin","f001"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s02; BRANCH=tx-cow-head-realloc; Search only snapshots/s02 and never open any other snapshot. Transmit/edit-path ownership analogue: tunnel xmit, neighbor output, netfilter mangle/targets, encapsulation, and header-edit helpers that store a pointer into skb head/data or protocol headers and then invoke skb_cow_head()/skb_cow()/skb_unclone()/skb_share_check()/pskb_expand_head()/skb_linearize() — any of which may free and replace skb->head — and afterwards use the stored pointer instead of refetching from skb->data. The broken invariant is identical to the seed: dereferencing a pointer into a buffer that a later call may reallocate or free. Record exact file:function:line evidence (capture, reallocating call, stale use) per candidate or an evidence-backed negative. Save a structured artifact for snapshot s02 only."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["origin","f001"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s02; BRANCH=loop-parser-stale-state; Search only snapshots/s02 and never open any other snapshot. State-transition analogue: TLV/option/record parse loops and next-record helpers where a pull or linearize (pskb_may_pull(), pskb_pull(), __pskb_pull_tail(), skb_linearize(), or a fetch inside a helper) happens inside the loop body or helper while pointer/offset/length state captured earlier remains live across the boundary and is dereferenced in a later iteration or after the helper returns — the exact shape of the seed's pep_get_sb() use-after-free. Hunt iterators whose local header pointer crosses a may_pull and helpers that both pull and leave outer-scope pointers stale. Record exact file:function:line evidence or an evidence-backed negative. Save a structured artifact for snapshot s02 only."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["origin","f001"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s03; BRANCH=rx-pull-stale-hdr; Search only snapshots/s03 and never open any other snapshot. Direct structural/API analogue of the seed: receive-path protocol parsers (net/* *_rcv, *_recv, *_do_rcv, *_rx handlers) that capture a header pointer via skb_header_pointer() or a direct skb->data cast, call pskb_may_pull()/pskb_pull()/__pskb_pull_tail()/skb_linearize() to linearize, and then dereference the pre-pull pointer (read or write) without refetching — the pep_get_sb() UAF shape. Also check parsers that pull a variable amount derived from the packet itself and then keep using an earlier header pointer. Record exact file:function:line evidence (capture, reallocating pull, post-pull uses) or an evidence-backed negative of what was searched. Save a structured artifact for snapshot s03 only."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["origin","f001"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s03; BRANCH=tx-cow-head-realloc; Search only snapshots/s03 and never open any other snapshot. Lifetime/ownership analogue on TX/edit paths: xmit handlers, neighbor output, netfilter mangle/target code, encapsulation, and header-rewrite helpers that cache pointers into skb head/data, network header, MAC header, or private headers across skb_cow_head()/skb_cow()/skb_unclone()/skb_share_check()/pskb_expand_head()/skb_linearize() calls that can free and reallocate skb->head, then write or read through the stale pointer without refetching. Remember pskb_expand_head() frees the old data area. Record exact file:function:line evidence (capture, reallocation, stale use) per candidate or an evidence-backed negative. Save a structured artifact for snapshot s03 only."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["origin","f001"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s03; BRANCH=loop-parser-stale-state; Search only snapshots/s03 and never open any other snapshot. Loop/helper stale-state analogue: variable-length record, TLV, option, and attribute parse loops plus 'get next record' helpers in which pskb_may_pull()/pskb_pull()/__pskb_pull_tail()/skb_linearize() runs inside the loop or helper while pointer, cursor, offset, or length state captured before the pull survives and is dereferenced afterwards — a state transition through freed slab memory exactly like the seed's pep_get_sb(). Look for while-loops over options with cached header pointers and next_*() iterators that pull internally. Record exact file:function:line evidence of captured state, interior pull, and stale use, or an evidence-backed negative. Save a structured artifact for snapshot s03 only."}
